{"id":"resp_ac44d3c135dba97d","created_at":1795550798,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9cf32c1870211e36","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shapes representing the supplied requirement: Category A ship definition, linking shipCategory property to polarShipCategoryA, and designIceCondition to mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions. Also need to encode that Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first-year ice, which may include old ice inclusions.\n\nWe have ontology terms: shipCategory (object property) domain ship, range polarShipCategoryValue. Also designIceCondition (object property) domain ship, range iceConditionValue.\n\nWe have individuals: polarShipCategoryA, mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions.\n\nRequirement: For a ship to be Category A, its shipCategory must be polarShipCategoryA AND its designIceCondition must be mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions. The text: \"Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first-year ice, which may include old ice inclusions.\"\n\nThus we need shape that validates ships with both properties matching those values. Use SHACL targetClass: https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship (as per admission schema). But the instruction says do not invent targets; we have explicit owner_class = ship, but target must be scoped class target permitted only with that mandatory input guard; we have that. So shape applies to instances of ship.\n\nDefine a sh:NodeShape with targetClass ship, and have two sh:property constraints:\n\n- sh:path shipCategory, sh:hasValue polarShipCategoryA, sh:message \"...\".\n\n- sh:path designIceCondition, sh:hasValue mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions, sh:message \"...\".\n\nAlso we may need constraint to ensure both hold simultaneously? Could be separate constraints; both must be satisfied.\n\nInclude source references as sh:source? Not standard. Could use sh:description with citation.\n\nAlso include provenance info? Not required.\n\nMake sure to use exact IRIs. Use prefixes maybe declare prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> and qdt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> maybe not needed.\n\nBecause no quantities.\n\nReturn <BEGIN_SHACL> line then Turtle.\n\nThus the Turtle:\n\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n\nnltl:ShipCategoryARequirementShape a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:description \"Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first-year ice, which may include old ice inclusions (IMO-001, IMO_POLAR_CODE p.9, 2.1).\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shipCategory ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:polarShipCategoryA ;\n        sh:message \"Ship must be classified as Category A.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:designIceCondition ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions ;\n        sh:message \"Design ice condition must be at least medium first-year ice with possible old ice inclusions.\" ;\n    ] .\n\nReturn.\n\nMake sure naming: shipCategory property is nltl:shipCategory, designIceCondition is nltl:designIceCondition.\n\nThus final answer.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_bcfe713f08cb01f0","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n\nnltl:ShipCategoryARequirementShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:description \"Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first‑year ice, which may include old ice inclusions. (IMO‑001 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.9 | 2.1)\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shipCategory ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:polarShipCategoryA ;\n        sh:message \"The ship must be classified as Category A (polarShipCategoryA).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:designIceCondition ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions ;\n        sh:message \"The design ice condition must be at least medium first‑year ice with possible old‑ice inclusions (mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions).\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":21317,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":21312,"cache_write_tokens":0,"input_tokens_per_turn":[21317],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[21312]},"output_tokens":1045,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":746,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1045],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":22362},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}